      "response": "Warning: Unknown toolsets: agency-runtime, async-delegation, messaging\n```python\ndef average(values):\n    if not values:\n        raise ValueError(\"average() requires at least one value\")\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n```\n\nCorrectness defects in the supplied function:\n- Uses `//`, so it floors/truncates the mean instead of returning fractional results.\n- Returns the wrong value for fractional means, e.g. `[1.0, 2.0]` gives `1.0` instead of `1.5`.\n- Empty input currently raises `ZeroDivisionError`; the requested contract is `ValueError`.\n\n```python\ndef test_average_fractional_floats():\n    assert average([1.0, 2.0]) == 1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_negative_numbers():\n    assert average([-1, -2, -3]) == -2\n\n\ndef test_average_empty_raises_value_error():\n    try:\n        average([])\n    except ValueError:\n        pass\n    else:\n        raise AssertionError(\"expected ValueError\")\n```\n\nNo files read or modified. Tests provided only; not executed.\n",
